# Access requirements

Permissions are granted per client. A person can hold several at once. Each permission grants only what it names. A page, menu entry, or API the person does not have stays closed, including when they open its URL directly.

When a new chat should follow this before editing access, say: read `.cursor/rules/access-requirements.mdc` before making changes.

## Stored roles

Each permission is a `role` on `client_user_roles` for one client. `ADMIN` and `SUPER_ADMIN` grant every permission on that client. `web_users.is_super_admin` grants every permission on every client.

| Role | Permission |
| --- | --- |
| `COMMISSION_TRACKER_READ` | Commission Tracker Read |
| `COMMISSION_TRACKER_WRITE` | Commission Tracker Write, which includes Read. It can read and write `client_caps`. |
| `COMMISSION_TRACKER_SETTINGS` | Commission Tracker Settings. It can also read and write `client_caps`. |
| `OWNER_REPORTS` | Owner Reports |
| `ADMIN` | Every permission on that client |
| `SUPER_ADMIN` | Every permission on that client |

Any active role on a client can read `client_caps`. Writing that table requires Commission Tracker Write, Commission Tracker Settings, `ADMIN`, `SUPER_ADMIN`, or platform super admin. `client_caps` holds team caps and agent caps.

## Permissions

### Commission Tracker Read

View Transactions and Agents. This permission cannot create, edit, or delete any record. On Transactions it does not show New Transaction, Sync with TMS, the sync highlight control, bulk select, the TMS connection column, the commission template column, Delete Transaction, the template control, Reset waterfall, Edit Transaction Overview, or Edit Commission Waterfall. On Agents it does not show New Agent, Edit Agent, or Delete Agent.

### Commission Tracker Write

Full use of Transactions and Agents, including creating, editing, and deleting. This permission includes read access to those two pages. It can read commission templates, parameters, and rules, and it can create, change, and delete commission template submissions. It can run Sync with TMS. It can read and write `client_caps`. It does not open Settings and cannot change template definitions or the spreadsheet connection.

### Commission Tracker Settings

Full use of Commission Tracker Settings, including viewing and changing those pages. It does not open Transactions, Agents, or any report.

### Owner Reports

Full use of Owner Reports, including viewing and filtering. It does not open Commission Tracker or any other report set.

### Super Admin

Every permission, including the deferred ones once those modules exist. A Super Admin does not need the other permissions granted separately.

## Deferred permissions

Do not build these until the module exists. Record them so the names stay reserved.

- **Agent Reports Admin.** View and filter Agent Reports for every agent.
- **Agent Reports Agent.** View and filter Agent Reports for that person's own agent data.
- **Office Reports.** View and filter Office Reports.
- **Goals.** Access to Goals.
- **Leads.** Access to Leads.
- **Operating Expenses.** Access to Operating Expenses.

## Clients

A person assigned to one client enters the app on that client.

A person assigned to more than one client must choose a client before any page, menu, or data is available. They can switch client without signing out. The choice lasts until they switch again. After a switch, the app shows that client's records and applies that client's permissions.

The top navigation shows that person the active client as a grey label pill beside the avatar (on phones left of search, showing the client's short code, such as DEMO or TATH, instead of the full name). It is only a label; switching stays in the profile menu.

The active client is one cookie shared by every tab of the browser. When a person switches client in one tab, every other open tab is told at once (and each tab checks again whenever it comes back into view): a tab still showing the previous client is covered by a notice, Client Changed in Another Tab, with Reload in the new client (on a page for one record, such as a transaction or a template, that button opens the record's list instead, Open Transactions in the new client, since the new client does not have that record) or Switch Back to the one it shows, so nothing in it is saved or loaded for the wrong client. Owner Reports in such a tab stops its background refreshes until then (`components/access-provider.tsx`). Working in two clients side by side would need the client sent by each tab instead of the shared cookie; that is not built.
